            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "EcoDataCenter secures 600 million euros to expand AI data centres",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "(Reuters) -Swedish digital infrastructure provider EcoDataCenter has secured 600 million euros ($703.5 million) in debt financing from Deutsche Bank  to expand its AI data centres, it said on Tuesday, as demand for high-performance computing surges amid the AI boom.  The funding, provided by Deutsche Bank through its Private Credit and Infrastructure unit, will accelerate the construction of large-scale data centres in Falun and Borlange, north of Stockholm, designed to support AI workloads and other compute-intensive applications.  CEO Peter Michelson, a former Ericsson executive, told Reuters that the funding would provide the company with a two-year runway within its current plans, but added that as demand continues to soar, the company was likely to expand further.",
